                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Atherstone was a music teacher in Taunton and later wrote poetry and a novel 
      about King Alfred. He was a close friend of <persName key="MAR03">John Martin's</persName>, at whose home many of his contacts 
      with Godwin take place. Godwin usually misses off the end 'e', but the pattern of use 
      strongly supports the view that Atherston and Atherstone are the same person. </p>
